# No Copied Content - Ever

When the user provides HTML, text, or screenshots from another website as a **reference**, they are showing you the FORMAT and STRUCTURE to replicate — never the actual words.

## Rules

- NEVER copy or paraphrase text from a competitor or reference website into any page, component, or data file.
- When given competitor content as a reference, extract only the **pattern** (layout, section types, data structure, link placement) and write 100% original content.
- This applies to descriptions, alt text, headings, list items, paragraphs — all user-facing text.
- The same real-world entities (attractions, schools, parks) can be linked, but descriptions MUST be written from scratch in original language.

## Why This Matters (SEO)

- Google already has the competitor's content indexed. Duplicating it provides zero ranking value and can trigger duplicate content penalties.
- Original content is the only content that earns organic ranking.
- "Match this kind of content" means match the structure, not the words.

## Before Writing Any Content

1. Is this text original, or did I pull phrasing from a reference the user provided?
2. Would this paragraph appear in a plagiarism check against the reference source?
3. If yes to either — rewrite from scratch.
